  "raw": " Tito made an announcement that no one expected:\n\nThe Bulgarian-Russian people intimately identify themselves with full culpability for the tragic events of March 1917; without excessive vitiation they will never abandon their cause, in its true character… Finally… Finally it is seeing free nationalization that the Bulgarians desire; that is all that boils within them. They ask only this, the task being finally done. Such is where we come from! They cannot refrain from bitter tears at seeing before their eyes their old country valiantly defended by Russian Blood… Finally Bulgaria went on her death march [and at last] became proletarian Russia, in fact the first de Bestia.” (Tito, “Message from the Fatherland”):\n\nDespite allegations that the leadership had plotted a coup against Lenin since the October Revolution, the truth is somewhat more complex. Accordingly, there was confusion among the Soviet Class insistence that no policies would be changed due to a break between the leaders was",
